{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104624","id":2417754271,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6QHACf","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104624","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104624.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104624.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104624","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104624/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104624/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104624/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/66b40a710f586dbef3a4e41b2101c580b545ad28","number":104624,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Project manager: Add option to backup project when it will be changed","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The goal is to allow users to easily backup their projects if Godot will make irreversible changes to them. While this could make it more likely that folks will make backups in general, I'm mainly thinking about Android where managing files at all can be difficult (or require installing additional apps to make it not difficult).\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2292\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\n### Opening an Old Project\r\n\r\nIf opening a project will lead to irreversible changes, it adds a \"Backup project first\" checkbox:\r\n\r\n![Selection_317](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d0c2706b-fb71-4407-b0d6-e2b48d3eaa49)\r\n\r\nIf you check it and click \"OK\" (or \"Full Conversion\" if opening a Godot 3 project), then it'll take the user to a variation on the usual dialog for creating a project, in order to allow them to pick the directory and name the project:\r\n\r\n![Selection_318](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a185ebf-e3d4-45e6-b6e8-ddaf5853acbf)\r\n\r\nAfter clicking \"Duplicate\", it will duplicate the project, but then continue on to open the original project.\r\n\r\n### Duplicating a project directly\r\n\r\nThis PR also adds a \"Duplicate\" button to the right sidebar:\r\n\r\n![Selection_315](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/091f50ff-3f9a-40cf-8e1e-93ee343c9b03)\r\n\r\nIf the user selects a project, and then clicks this \"Duplicate\" button, it'll take the user to a variation on the usual dialog for creating a project similar to the one shown above:\r\n\r\n![Selection_316](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/44b30bb9-f276-415b-9918-2057436b6839)\r\n\r\nHowever, this time it includes the \"Edit Now\" checkbox, which if checked, will lead to the newly duplicated project to be opened. If not, it only does the duplication, and then closes this dialog, returning the user to the list of projects.\r\n\r\n## Caveats\r\n\r\n- There is no progress dialog when copying the project: it just freezes until the copy is finished. However, it does the same thing when extracting a project from a ZIP file. We probably should have a progress dialog here for both installing from ZIP and project duplication, but since this matches pre-existing behavior, it seems like something that can be handled in a future PR\r\n\r\n## Original List of Alternative Approaches\r\n\r\n**UPDATE (2025-04-07):** The current PR now implements alternatives nr 1 and 2. I'm just keeping this section here so that early comments referring to these approaches still make sense :-)\r\n\r\n1. Rather than sneaking in a \"Backup Project\" button into the dialog when changes are possible, we could have a \"Copy Project\" project button on the side and it'd be up to the user to use that button on their own. This takes the user out of the flow, so they may be less likely to do it, but it would be less weird that the project doesn't get opened immediately after completing the backup. Mockup:\r\n    ![Selection_307](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/21b0e041-1b84-4faf-9429-70adebcb3720)\r\n2. Rather than being a button, there could be a \"Make a backup first\" checkbox in the dialog. Then regardless of which button the user clicks, it'll go to the dialog to make the backup, and then afterwards proceed to opening the project. Mockup:\r\n    ![Selection_308](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b2cbf96d-b8ea-4793-88a3-2d21437a32be)\r\n3. Rather than making a copy of the old project, and then opening the original (upgrading it), should this open the copy (leaving the original alone)? I was torn on which way to go, and I'm not sure I picked the right one. I guess if you think of the upgraded project as a continuation of the original, it's nice for that to be in the same directory going forward?\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MD